  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>AntibesDogz is a family boarding service for dogs in the Rabiac district, north of Antibes. Your dog lives with the family and other dogs, in a large heated and air-conditioned villa with a fully fenced garden, under 24-hour video surveillance. The boarding is ACACED-certified and covered by professional liability insurance.</p>
      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Boarding costs €32 per day for one dog, €54 for two and €76 for three dogs kept together. The price includes walks in the surrounding parks, giving medication if needed, special diets on request, and photos and news by WhatsApp. AntibesDogz can also pick up and bring back your dog at your home, from €29 round trip between Antibes and the surrounding area. In an emergency, the boarding works with a nearby vet (vet fees extra).</p>
      <p>You start with a visit to the boarding, to be booked by email or phone. Note that the boarding is closed from 19 December 2026 to 10 January 2027 inclusive.</p>
      <h2>Admission conditions for your dog</h2>
      <p>The house rules are precise. Your dog must be identified (microchip or tattoo), have an up-to-date health record, which stays at the boarding during the stay, and vaccines given at least fifteen days earlier: distemper, Rubarth's hepatitis, leptospirosis, parvovirus and kennel cough. It must also be dewormed and treated against external parasites before arrival.</p>
      <p>Males must be neutered. Category 1 and 2 dogs, aggressive, dominant or guard-trained dogs, and animals with a contagious disease are not accepted. An assessment appointment checks that your dog gets on with the other guests, and the boarding reserves the right to refuse admission after this meeting. Any treatment must come with a valid veterinary prescription.</p>
      <h2>Hours, arrivals and emergencies</h2>
      <p>Late arrivals after 8pm are not charged, and a day that has started is not counted if you collect your dog before 10am. Prices are firm, without VAT (sole proprietorship). The veterinarian designated by the boarding is the Clinique vétérinaire des Clausonnes, in Valbonne, whose rules state 24/7 opening; in an emergency, the boarding can also take your dog to your usual vet.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: use the visit to introduce your dog and see the garden, then think about transport if you leave early: it is often simpler than making the round trip yourself.</div>
      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The boarding is in the Rabiac district of Antibes. Daily walks take place in the neighbouring parks, a few minutes from the boarding, and the boarding says it takes your dog to the park adjoining the property.</p>
